sentences.l:
He answered, saying: “How would Ci dare look toward Hui?
Hui hears one and by it knows ten;
Ci hears one and by it knows two.”

The Master said of Zichan: “Of the gentleman's ways he had four in him:
in conducting himself, respectful;
in serving superiors, reverent;
in nurturing the people, kind;
in employing the people, right.”

The Master said: “Ning Wuzi:
when the state had the Way, then he was wise;
when the state lacked the Way, then he was foolish.
His wisdom can be reached;
his foolishness cannot be reached.”

The Master said: “Who calls Weisheng Gao straight?
Someone asked him for vinegar;
he asked his neighbour for some and handed it on.”

The Master said: “Clever words, a pleasing face, overdone courtesy —
Zuo Qiuming was ashamed of them;
I, Qiu, am ashamed of them too.
Hiding resentment and befriending the man —
Zuo Qiuming was ashamed of it;
I, Qiu, am ashamed of it too.”

Zilu said: “We wish to hear your aims, Master.”
The Master said: “The old — to give them ease;
friends — to keep faith with them;
the young — to hold them close.”
